### Sanity configuration - replace with your own values after running sanity:init
PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID="your sanity project id here"
PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET="production"
SANITY_STUDIO_STUDIO_HOST="your sanity studio host here"

### Customize the following variables to match your site details
PUBLIC_PAGE_TITLE="in the browser tab title"
PUBLIC_NAVBAR_TITLE="what you want in the navbar"
PUBLIC_COPYRIGHT_HOLDER="your name or your company's name here"

### Deployment (Cloudflare Workers)
# Deploys run in Cloudflare Workers Builds, not locally and not in CI here.
# The build-time values (SANITY_*, PUBLIC_*) are configured as environment
# variables on the Worker in the Cloudflare dashboard — this file is only for
# running the site, the Studio and `npm run preview:cf` locally.
#
# `npm run deploy:cf` / `wrangler` on your own machine uses the OAuth login in
# ~/.config/.wrangler, so no token is needed here. CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID is only
# required if wrangler cannot infer the account from that login.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID="your cloudflare account id here"
#
# Self-hosting (Docker + Dokploy) is still possible from the `self-host` branch;
# that branch's .env.example documents DOKPLOY_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL and the
# CF-Access-Client-Id/Secret pair it needs.
